    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 BorderKeys contributors

    The core mark with a badge on it, because the two builds can now be installed side by side
    and a launcher full of identical icons is a launcher you have to read.

    The badge sits on the lower right of the space bar rather than in the corner of the canvas.
    A corner is exactly what an adaptive icon does not have: the launcher applies its own mask,
    and only the middle 66 of the 108 units are guaranteed to survive it. Centred at 70,64 with
    a radius of 11, the badge's farthest point is 33 units from the centre, inside the
    guarantee, so it is never the part a round mask takes off.

    It is punched out of the bar rather than drawn over it: the disc is the pale key colour and
    the cross is the background, which reads at the size a folder shrinks this to. A thin
    stroke over a light bar would not.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

